.\" Manual page for docmost-cli-sync(1)
.\" Source: SPECIFICATION.md section 4.10, src/docmost_cli/cli/sync_cmd.py
.TH DOCMOST\-CLI\-SYNC 1 "2026\-03\-22" "docmost\-cli 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docmost\-cli\-sync \- synchronize Docmost pages with local Markdown files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docmost\-cli sync pull
.I space\-slug
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli sync push
.I space\-slug
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli sync status
.I space\-slug
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The sync commands enable documentation\-as\-code workflows by maintaining
a local directory of Markdown files that mirrors a Docmost space.
.PP
Each page is stored as a single Markdown file with YAML frontmatter
containing page metadata.
A
.I .docmost\-manifest.json
file tracks local Markdown hashes and canonical SHA\-256 fingerprints of raw
server page state for change detection.
.SS Local directory format
After
.BR "sync pull" ,
the target directory contains:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
engineering/
  Getting Started\-\-019a2a69.md
  API Reference\-\-019b3c8f.md
  files/019c4d9a\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxxxxxxxxxx/diagram.png
  .docmost/raw\-pages/019a2a69\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxxxxxxxxxx.json
  .docmost\-manifest.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Each file is named
.IB title \-\- id\-prefix .md
and contains YAML frontmatter:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\-\-\-
id: 019a2a69\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxx\-xxxxxxxxxxxx
title: Getting Started
parent_id: null
icon: null
\-\-\-

# Getting Started

Page content here...
.EE
.RE
.SS Attachment assets
Referenced page attachments are downloaded beneath
.IR files/ attachment\-id / filename
and tracked by owner plus SHA\-256 hash in the manifest.
Push uploads new local file/image links and replaces changed attachment bytes
in place, preserving stable attachment and page IDs on both editions.
.SS Rich content safety
Pull uses Docmost's server\-side Markdown conversion and stores the exact
same\-revision ProseMirror JSON beneath
.IR .docmost/raw\-pages/ .
Concurrent page changes detected during pull are retried.
The manifest records editor features that Markdown cannot preserve, including
mentions, comments, columns, transclusions, embeds, alignment, colors, and
merged table cells.
.PP
Before any server mutation, push checks every content and attachment replacement.
If the source page contains a protected feature, the complete push stops with
page\-level diagnostics and the raw snapshot path.
Title, icon, and parent\-only changes remain allowed because they do not replace
page content.
.PP
Manifests created by older CLI versions remain usable.
Run a fresh pull to add raw snapshots and enable the rich\-content guard for
their existing pages.
If a successful server response contains no canonical Markdown, pull writes
compatibility output for reading but protects that page from content replacement.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS pull
Download all pages from a space to local Markdown files.
.PP
.I space\-slug
identifies the space to pull from.
.PP
Creates a directory with one
.I .md
file per page (with YAML frontmatter) and a
.I .docmost\-manifest.json
tracking sync state.
.PP
The complete pull is downloaded and validated in a sibling staging directory
before publication. If a page, attachment, validation, or filesystem operation
fails, the previous sync remains in place.
.PP
If the target changes while downloads are in progress, pull aborts without
overwriting the intervening edits. Publication uses an atomic directory exchange
where supported and a durable recovery journal on portable fallback paths.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " path"
Target directory.
Default:
.BI ./ space\-slug /
in the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace the files tracked by the previous manifest without prompting.
Stale tracked pages and attachments, including remotely renamed pages,
are removed. Files not tracked by the manifest are preserved.
Without this flag, a directory with an existing sync manifest is rejected.
.SS push
Upload local changes to the Docmost server.
.PP
.I space\-slug
identifies the space to push changes to.
.PP
Requires a prior
.B sync pull
to establish the manifest.
Content replacement is refused when the pull\-time guard shows that Markdown
would discard rich editor features.
Guarded pages are fetched again immediately before replacement so rich content
added in Docmost after the last pull is also protected.
Prompts for confirmation before applying changes unless
.B \-\-yes
or
.B \-\-dry\-run
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " path"
Source directory.
Default:
.BI ./ space\-slug /
in the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what changes would be applied without executing them.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete server pages that are not found locally.
Without this flag, pages deleted from the local directory are
left untouched on the server.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Apply local changes even when the server page changed since the last pull.
Without this flag, push checks every page to be updated, moved, or deleted
against its raw
.B /pages/info
revision before making any mutation and aborts the entire push on conflict.
Locally changed tracked attachments also compare the current remote bytes with
their stored pulled fingerprint before replacing attachment bytes in place.
Forced conflicting pages keep their previous baseline; reconcile before the
next normal push.
.PP
The revision check is a best\-effort preflight, not atomic compare\-and\-swap.
Current Docmost page mutation endpoints do not accept a conditional revision
token, so a remote edit racing after the check can still be overwritten.
.PP
Manifests created before remote revision tracking remain readable, but their
existing pages require reconciliation or an explicit
.B sync push \-\-force
before mutation.
.PP
To reconcile safely, preserve local edits and pull the remote space into a
separate directory with
.BR "sync pull " space\-slug " \-\-dir " new\-directory .
Merge the two copies instead of force\-pulling over active local files.
.SS status
Show changes between local files and the last\-pulled state.
.PP
.I space\-slug
identifies the space to check.
.PP
Displays a summary of new, modified, moved, deleted, and unchanged files
by comparing current file content hashes against the manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " path"
Directory to check.
Default:
.BI ./ space\-slug /
in the current working directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Pull a space to a local directory:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync pull engineering
$ docmost\-cli sync pull engineering \-\-dir ./docs/eng
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check what has changed locally:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync status engineering
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview changes before pushing:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync push engineering \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Push changes (with confirmation prompt):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync push engineering
.EE
.RE
.PP
Push changes non\-interactively, deleting removed pages:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli \-y sync push engineering \-\-delete
.EE
.RE
.PP
Deliberately apply local changes after reviewing a remote conflict:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync push engineering \-\-force
.EE
.RE
.PP
Typical docs\-as\-code workflow:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli sync pull engineering \-\-dir ./docs/
$ $EDITOR docs/Getting\\ Started\-\-019a2a69.md
$ docmost\-cli sync status engineering \-\-dir ./docs/
$ docmost\-cli sync push engineering \-\-dir ./docs/
.EE
.RE
